│     └─6 text " will fail since it\nmatches a directory."
├─53  heading[1]
│     │ depth: 2
│     └─0 text "Jupyter Notebook discovery"
├─54  paragraph[5]
│     ├─0 text "Ruff has built-in support for linting and formatting "
│     ├─1 link[1]
│     │   │ title: null
│     │   │ url: "https://jupyter.org/"
│     │   └─0 text "Jupyter Notebooks"
│     ├─2 text ",\nwhich are linted and formatted by default on version "
│     ├─3 inlineCode "0.6.0"
│     └─4 text " and higher."
├─55  paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "If you'd prefer to either only lint or only format Jupyter Notebook files, you can use the\nsection-specific "
│     ├─1 inlineCode "exclude"
│     └─2 text " option to do so. For example, the following would only lint Jupyter\nNotebook files and not format them:"
├─56  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "=== \"pyproject.toml\""
├─57  code "```toml\n[tool.ruff.format]\nexclude = [\"*.ipynb\"]\n```"
│       lang: null
│       meta: null
├─58  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "=== \"ruff.toml\""
├─59  code "```toml\n[format]\nexclude = [\"*.ipynb\"]\n```"
│       lang: null
│       meta: null
├─60  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "And, conversely, the following would only format Jupyter Notebook files and not lint them:"
├─61  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "=== \"pyproject.toml\""
├─62  code "```toml\n[tool.ruff.lint]\nexclude = [\"*.ipynb\"]\n```"
│       lang: null
│       meta: null
├─63  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "=== \"ruff.toml\""
├─64  code "```toml\n[lint]\nexclude = [\"*.ipynb\"]\n```"
│       lang: null
│       meta: null
├─65  paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "You can completely disable Jupyter Notebook support by updating the\n"
│     ├─1 link[1]
│     │   │ title: null
│     │   │ url: "settings.md#extend-exclude"
│     │   └─0 inlineCode "extend-exclude"
│     └─2 text " setting:"
├─66  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "=== \"pyproject.toml\""
├─67  code "```toml\n[tool.ruff]\nextend-exclude = [\"*.ipynb\"]\n```"
│       lang: null
│       meta: null
├─68  paragraph[1]
